<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF unit wins German army order.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF unit wins German army order.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>French defence electronics firm Thomson-CSF said on Tuesday its Thomson Training &amp; Simulation subsidiary has won its largest-ever order for its infantry training weapons simulator with a contract for the German army.</p>
<p>The multi-million pound order is for 142 systems to be delivered over two years beginning November 1997, it said in a statement.</p>
</text>
